Task: Phase 0 / Schema gap fix (Track 1 follow-up)

Discovery:
Pilot route (app/api/lessons/[lessonSlug]/route.ts) calls
prisma.lesson.findUnique({ include: { standards, curriculumUnits: { include: { class: { include: { teacher, students } } } } } }).
Track 1's audit classified Lesson/Standard/CurriculumUnit/Class as PORT-AS-IS but
never modeled the four implicit Prisma join tables in Drizzle. Without them, every
M:N relation in science-advantage (standards, students, units) is unrepresentable.

Decision:
Per user direction, fix inside Track 3 Phase 0 (not a Track 1 reopen). Faster and
keeps junction definitions co-located with the controllers that use them.

Tables added (all composite-PK, both FKs ON DELETE CASCADE to mirror Prisma):
  - science_lesson_standards    (lesson_id, standard_id)
  - science_unit_lessons        (unit_id, lesson_id)
  - science_class_students      (class_id, student_id)   -- student_id is text (FK to users.id)
  - science_question_standards  (question_id, standard_id)

